  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` to `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as 9159c2d. The four new tests in `test/cli/truncate.test.ts` pass when run with `node --test`. I did not run the full `npm test` suite.\n\n- **Behavior:** Text of `max` characters or fewer comes back unchanged. Longer text keeps its start and end around a single `…`, and the result is never longer than `max`. When the kept characters can't split evenly, the start gets the extra one, so `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 6)` gives `abc…ij`.\n- **Small `max`:** `max` of 0 or less gives an empty string, and `max` of 1 gives just `…`.\n- **Counting:** Length is counted in Unicode code points, so characters outside the basic range aren't split in half.\n- **Tests:** I put the test file in `test/cli/`, next to the other CLI tests. It covers short text, a normal truncation, the length limit across `max` values 0 to 11, and tiny `max` values.",
